o Sunday and see wins and losses  and they need to go through a that's  like I get it but I guess I'm the kind  of person that is I'm gonna put we're  gonna put the work in we're gonna be  ready to go we're looking to win so  that's that's kind of our mindset that's  what we're looking to do we have  expectations as a coaching staff we have  expectations as players and we're going  to look to meet those expectations April  when the schedule comes out who do you  want week one Patriots or the Dolphins  ooh I I'm not gonna Mike you can't you  can decide that you  I'm not gonna I'm not gonna do all right  I think I know I think I know I'm a guy  take the Dolphins every week for 17  weeks including the bye week  oh that's just I want Obama I'm all for  bye week I've gone through one of those  16 straight weeks of stuff that's true  that's right that was one of the things  that hung over that season in 2017  people say what went wrong what went  wrong is everything went wrong for the  Dolphins that year I mean it's not an  excuse it's a reality so hopefully  you'll have your starting quarterback  for a full season hopefully you won't  have games moved around and by weeks  taken away and hopefully you'll have  fewer of the adversities that you had to  deal with the last two years in Miami  coach appreciate some of your time all  the best going forward look forward to  talking to you down the road I  appreciate it Mike  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports
 

